2. CRITERION-1 ARITHMETIC — PASS
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Read from source (metrics.go): TotalIncome/TotalExpenses/NetSavings/
SavingsRate are computed ABOVE the exclusion, and the only subtraction is
    livingTotal := totalExpenses - healthcareTotal - planExcludedTotal
so the design constraint holds structurally, not by luck.

TESTS ASSERT IT, and I proved they are load-bearing rather than reading them:
  MUT A_living — drop `- planExcludedTotal`:
    --- FAIL: TestCalculateMetrics_PlanExclusions_DropsLivingByExactFlaggedNetTotalExpensesUnchanged
        plan_exclusions_test.go:62: LivingExpensesTotal drop = 0, want 600 (the flagged net exactly)
        plan_exclusions_test.go:65: LivingExpensesTotal (with flag) = 4100, want 3500
    --- FAIL: TestCalculateMetrics_PlanExclusions_CombinedCumulativeBalanceInvariantHolds
    --- FAIL: TestComparison_PlanExclusionsAppliedToBothWindows
  MUT A_trend — drop the per-month `- excludedAmt`:
    --- FAIL: ..._LivingTrendExcludesFlaggedMonth
        plan_exclusions_test.go:184: LivingExpensesTrend[Jan] = 2100, want 1500
  MUT A_walk — drop the combined-cumulative walk's spend subtraction:
    --- FAIL: ..._CombinedCumulativeBalanceInvariantHolds
        last CombinedCumulativeBalance point = -1395.48..., want -795.48... (== -CombinedCumulativeDelta)
  MUT A_hi2 — disable the HI-first skip in PlanExcludedOutflows (D-SY-e):
    --- FAIL: ..._HIOverlapExcludedOnceNotDoubleSubtracted
        PlanExcludedTotal = 700, want 0 ; PlanExcludedCount = 1, want 0
        LivingExpensesTotal = 2300, want 3000 (the overlap row must not be subtracted twice)
  MUT A_cmp — pass nil to the COMPARISON window only inside Comparison:
    --- FAIL: TestComparison_PlanExclusionsAppliedToBothWindows
        Previous.LivingExpensesTotal = 2100, want 1500
  Every arm of the living arithmetic — range total, per-month trend, combined
  walk, HI ordering, and both Comparison windows — dies under the mutation
  that breaks exactly it.

TOTALS UNCHANGED: plan_exclusions_test.go:42-56 asserts TotalExpenses,
TotalIncome, NetSavings AND SavingsRate are identical with-flag vs
without-flag on the same fixture, plus an absolute pin
(`TotalExpenses = 4100 ... flag never removes a dollar of real spend`).

NIL == EMPTY == PRE-CHANGE FOR EVERY FIELD: the test uses a genuine golden
comparison, not a field checklist that could omit one —
    withNil  := Calculate(..., nil)
    withEmpty:= Calculate(..., map[string]models.MajorExpense{})
    if !reflect.DeepEqual(withNil, withEmpty) { ... }
and a THIRD case (a map whose only key matches no transaction Hash) also
DeepEqual'd against nil. reflect.DeepEqual follows both *DashboardMetrics
pointers, so this covers every field including the new ones — exactly what
criterion 5(b) asks.

